# The plain builtin, which agreed on the two native engines and diverged on the
# page — `rt_truthy` is what both `if` and a guard reach there, so one wrong
# sentence covered both constructs and nothing walked either.
#
# The condition is a STRING because the page's old sentence differed in two
# ways and an int shows only one: `if takes a bool condition (got "x")` is the
# other wording AND the other rendering, where an int reads `7` on all three.
pub fn opaque v
  v

pub play = print "{if (opaque "x") "a" "b"}"
